hadiths[37]{hadithnumber,text}:
"394","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to give glad tidings to his noble companions (may Allah be pleased with them) saying: “A blessed month, Ramadan, has come to you. Allah has made its fasting obligatory upon you. In it, the gates of Paradise are opened and the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained. In it, there is a night (Laylat al-Qadr) which is better than a thousand months (of worship). Whoever is deprived of its goodness has truly been deprived (in every respect).”"
"395","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blessed month of Ramadan has come to you."" Then he narrated similar to the previous hadith."
"396","It is narrated from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi that Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) was on a journey. He stopped at a place and sent a messenger to him while he was praying, so that he could come and eat. He said to the messenger: I am fasting. When the food was served and it was near that they would finish, he also started eating. Then he looked towards his messenger, so he said: He had told me that he was fasting. Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He spoke the truth. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Fasting in the month of patience and fasting three days of every month is equivalent to fasting forever."" I have already fasted three days of the month. I am one who leaves fasting in Allah’s concession and fasts in Allah’s strengthening."
"397","Abu Uthman al-Nahdi narrated: I hosted Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) for seven days; with him were his wife and his servant. They had assigned turns for the third parts of the night: one would stand (in prayer) while the other slept, and when this one stood, the other would sleep. And I heard Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) distributed dates, and my share was seven dates. Among them was one spoiled, dry date, and it was the most beloved to me; it made my chewing of the dates stronger. Sulaiman said: That is, it had strength. The narrator said: I asked, ""Abu Hurairah! How do you fast in the month?"" He replied: ""I fast three days at the beginning of the month, so if any issue arises for me, I have the reward for the whole month."""
"398","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""When any of you eats or drinks forgetfully while fasting, he should not break his fast but complete it, for it is Allah who has fed him and given him drink."""
"399","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats or drinks forgetfully should complete his fast, for it is Allah who has fed him and given him drink."""
"400","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Begin fasting upon sighting the moon, and stop fasting upon sighting the moon."" Or he said: ""When you see it, then begin fasting, and when you see (the Shawwal moon), then stop fasting. If the sky is cloudy for you, then complete the count to thirty."""
"401","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""When you see the (crescent of Ramadan), then fast, and when you see it (the crescent of Shawwal), then stop fasting. If the sky is cloudy, then complete the count to thirty."""
"402","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then the narrator mentioned it similar to the previous hadith, and said: ""If the sky is cloudy for you."""
"403","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah says, 'O son of Adam! Every deed is an expiation except for fasting; it (fasting) is for Me and I alone will reward it. The smell from the mouth of the fasting person is better with Allah than the fragrance of musk.'"""
"404","Muhammad bin Ziyad narrated, I heard Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate the same example from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"405","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Avoid wisal, avoid wisal, avoid wisal."" They said: O Messenger of Allah! You observe wisal (fasting continuously without breaking the fast), so he (peace be upon him) said: ""You are not like me in this matter. I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me drink. So perform only as many deeds as you have the strength for."""
"406","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves one fast of Ramadan without a (legal) concession, then even if he fasts for his entire life, it will not suffice for it."""
"407","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves one fast of Ramadan without a concession given by Allah, then even if he fasts for his entire life, it will not make up for it."""
"408","Abu Al-Mutawwas (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) the same narration, he said: ""Without any illness or permission."""
"409","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever leaves one fast of Ramadan without an allowance given by Allah, then fasting for a lifetime will not make up for it."""
"410","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates in a marfu’ form that it was asked from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): Which prayer is the best after the obligatory prayers? Which fast is the best after the fast of Ramadan? So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “After the obligatory prayer, the best prayer is a person’s prayer in the last third of the night, and after the fast of Ramadan, the best fast is the fast of Allah’s month, Muharram.”"
"411","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The most virtuous prayer after the obligatory prayers is the night prayer (Tahajjud), and the most virtuous fast after the fasts of Ramadan is the fast of Allah's month, Muharram."""
"412","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""The supplication of the fasting person is not rejected."""
"413","With the same (previous) chain, it is narrated from the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), he said: ""None of you should say, 'I have fasted the fast of Ramadan.'"""
"414","Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""None of you should say, 'I fasted the entire Ramadan and I stood (in prayer) the entire Ramadan.'"" The narrator said: I do not know whether he (the Prophet) liked self-purification or not. And he (peace be upon him) said: Sleeping or staying awake is necessary."
"415","With this same chain (as previous), the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever stands (in prayer) on the Night of Qadr with faith in Allah and affirming it, his previous sins are forgiven."""
"416","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Your fast is on the day when you (see the moon and) begin fasting, and your Eid al-Fitr is on the day when you (complete Ramadan and) stop fasting."""
"417","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""Friday is a day of Eid, so do not make your day of Eid a day of fasting, unless you fast a day before it or a day after it."""
"418","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""Do not fast on the day of Friday unless you join a fast with it (fast one day before or one day after)."""
"419","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the smell from the mouth of the fasting person will be better with Allah than the fragrance of musk."""
"420","Lady Rabi’ bint Mu’awwiz bin ‘Afra’ (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: On the morning of ‘Ashura, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a message to the settlements of the Ansar, and said: “Whoever among you has fasted today, let him complete his fast, and whoever among you has not fasted, let him fast for the rest of the day.”"
"421","Khubayb bin Abdur Rahman narrated from his paternal aunt, she heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) gives the adhan at night, or Ibn Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him) gives the adhan at night, so you should continue eating (the pre-dawn meal) until you hear the adhan of Ibn Umm Maktum or Bilal (may Allah be pleased with them). The only difference between the two was that one would descend (downstairs) and the other would ascend (to the roof). The narrator said: We used to say to them: Wait until we finish eating suhoor."
"422","Lady Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to our house, so I presented a drink to him, or it was presented to him, and he drank it. Then he handed it to me. I said: O Messenger of Allah! I am fasting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who keeps a voluntary fast is his own master (ruler); if you wish, complete your fast, and if you wish, break it."""
"423","Umar bin Khaldah Al-Ansari narrated from his mother (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) during the days of Tashreeq, so he announced that these are days of eating, drinking, and intimacy (with one's wife), not for fasting."
"424","It is narrated from Sayyida Umm al-Fadl (may Allah be pleased with her) that she sent milk to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the day of Arafah while he was delivering the sermon, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) drank it."
"425","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) traveled during Ramadan, and he observed the fast until he reached Usfan. Then he asked for a vessel in which there was a drink, and he drank it during the day so that people could see him. After that, he did not fast during the journey until he entered Makkah. Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has both fasted and not fasted during travel, so whoever wishes may fast and whoever wishes may not fast."
"426","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: We did not object to the fasting person or the one not fasting during travel. Wakī‘ (may Allah have mercy on him) added that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fasted during travel and also did not fast."
"427","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he (peace be upon him) said: ""We are a group of Prophets (peace be upon them all), we have been commanded to hasten in breaking the fast (at the time of iftar), to delay the pre-dawn meal (suhoor), and that we should hold our left hands with our right hands during prayer."""
"428","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man came to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: ""My mother has passed away, and she had a month of fasting due upon her. Should I fulfill it on her behalf?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tell me! If your mother had a debt, would you pay it off?"" He replied: ""Yes!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then Allah's debt is more deserving to be fulfilled."""
"429","Saeed bin Jubair (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith."
"430","Saeed bin Jubair (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) a narration similar to the previous hadith, and stated: He fulfilled (the fasts) on her (his mother's) behalf."
